.Dd August 9, 2026
.Dt LCTL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm lctl
.Nd a simpler CLI on top of launchctl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v | Fl \-verbose
.Op Fl y | Fl \-yes
.Op Ar command
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar args
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a simpler CLI on top of
.Xr launchctl 1 ,
forked from angel.
A friendlier CLI with lots of helpful features: services can live
wherever you want, more meaningful errors, and a status command.
It wraps common
.Xr launchctl 1
workflows for installing, starting, stopping,
restarting, listing, inspecting, and logging services.
.Pp
Without a
.Ar command ,
.Nm
lists your services, like
.Cm list .
.Pp
Service names may be matched fuzzily unless
.Fl e Ns / Ns Fl \-exact
is given.
.Sh GLOBAL OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl v , Fl \-verbose
Verbose output.
.It Fl y , Fl \-yes
Assume yes for confirmation prompts.
.It Fl h , Fl \-help
Print help.
.It Fl V , Fl \-version
Print version.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Ss install
Place a plist at
.Pa ~/Library/LaunchAgents/<label>.plist
.Pq Ar gui , Ar user
or
.Pa /Library/LaunchDaemons/<label>.plist
.Pq Ar system
and load it
.Pq Cm launchctl bootstrap .
If a service with the same label is loaded, it is unloaded first
.Pq Cm launchctl disable , bootout , enable
after confirmation.
For
.Ar system ,
the plist is made
.Ql root:wheel 644 ;
with the default symlink strategy that applies to your source file.
.Ar path
may also be the name of a plist in the lctl directory
.Pq see Sx CONFIGURATION .
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm install
.Op Fl s | Fl \-strategy Ar strategy
.Op Fl \-domain Ar domain
.Ar path
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl s , Fl \-strategy Ar strategy
How to place the plist:
.Ar copy ,
.Ar symlink
(default), or
.Ar move .
.It Fl \-domain Ar domain
Target domain:
.Ar gui ,
.Ar user ,
or
.Ar system .
Skips interactive domain selection.
.El
.Ss uninstall
Unload the service
.Pq Cm launchctl bootout , No best-effort ,
delete its plist (only the link if it is a symlink), and clear any disabled
flag
.Pq Cm launchctl enable , No best-effort .
Deleting a plist in
.Pa /Library/LaunchDaemons
needs root: run it under
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm uninstall
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Ar name
.Ss start
Start a service, loading it first
.Pq Cm launchctl bootstrap
if launchd does not have it loaded.
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm start
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Ar name
.Ss stop
Stop and unload a service
.Pq Cm launchctl bootout .
It stays stopped even with
.Cm KeepAlive ,
until it is started again or, for plists in a standard Launch* directory,
until the next login or boot.
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm stop
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Ar name
.Ss restart
Restart a service
.Pq Cm launchctl kickstart -k .
If it is not loaded, behave like
.Cm start .
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm restart
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Ar name
.Ss reload
Unload and load the service again.
Picks up plist edits and symlink target changes.
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm reload
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Ar name
.Ss status
Show one service on one screen: state, domain, enabled or disabled, PID,
the command it runs, when it runs, log files, plist path, problems found by
the checks of
.Cm doctor ,
and the next commands to run.
Calls
.Cm launchctl print
when the service is loaded.
Without a
.Ar name ,
same as
.Cm list .
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm status
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Op Fl d | Fl \-debug
.Op Ar name
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d , Fl \-debug
Also show every launchd field and the raw
.Cm launchctl print
output.
.El
.Ss logs
Show the last 50 lines of the plist's
.Cm StandardOutPath
and
.Cm StandardErrorPath
files, and of the unified log
.Pq Xr log 1 Cm show
for the service's program.
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm logs
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Op Fl t | Fl \-time Ar timeframe
.Ar name
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl t , Fl \-time Ar timeframe
Log time window, e.g.
.Ar 5m ,
.Ar 1h ,
.Ar 24h .
Default:
.Ar 5m .
.El
.Ss list
List services with their state (running, idle, failed, not loaded,
disabled), PID, domain, label, when they run, and plist path.
By default: services with a plist on disk that are not Apple's, in any state.
Alias:
.Cm ls .
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm list
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Op Fl a | Fl \-apple
.Op Fl d | Fl \-dynamic
.Op Fl \-running
.Op Fl \-idle
.Op Fl \-failed
.Op Fl \-not-loaded
.Op Fl \-disabled
.Op Fl 1 | Fl \-labels
.Op Fl s | Fl \-sort Ar field
.Op Ar pattern
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a , Fl \-apple
Include Apple services.
.It Fl d , Fl \-dynamic
Include services without a plist on disk.
.It Fl \-running , Fl \-idle , Fl \-failed , Fl \-not-loaded , Fl \-disabled
Only services in these states; can be combined.
.It Fl 1 , Fl \-labels
Print labels only, one per line.
.It Fl s , Fl \-sort Ar field
Sort by
.Ar parent ,
.Ar domain ,
or
.Ar name
(default).
.El
.Ss plist
Print the service's plist file (text plists only).
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm plist
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Ar name
.Ss enable
Clear the disabled override and load the service.
Persists across reboots.
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm enable
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Ar name
.Ss disable
Set the disabled override and unload the service.
Persists across reboots until
.Cm enable .
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm disable
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Ar name
.Ss doctor
Check plists and services for problems: missing Label, wrong owner or
permissions, missing or non-executable program, missing WorkingDirectory or
log directory, no launch trigger, very short StartInterval, and a loaded
definition that differs from the plist on disk.
Prints the command that fixes each problem when there is one.
Without a
.Ar name ,
checks all the services
.Cm list
shows by default and prints only those with problems
.Po
.Fl v :
all checks
.Pc .
Exits non-zero if a check fails.
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm doctor
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Op Ar name
.Ss explain
Print what
.Nm
runs under the hood: the
.Xr launchctl 1
commands behind each
.Nm
command, the
.Xr launchctl 1
to
.Nm
mapping, the install and uninstall steps, and the doctor checks.
This is the
.Dq How lctl maps to launchctl
section of the README, built into the binary.
With a
.Ar command ,
such as
.Cm stop
or the
.Xr launchctl 1
verb
.Cm load ,
it prints only the parts about that command.
Every
.Fl \-help
page ends with the matching
.Cm explain
command.
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm explain
.Op Ar command
.Sh COMMON OPTIONS
Most commands that take a service
.Ar name
accept:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl e , Fl \-exact
Require an exact name match instead of fuzzy matching.
.El
.Sh DOMAINS
.Nm
targets launchd domains the same way
.Xr launchctl 1
does:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar gui
Aqua / GUI login session
.Pq Cm gui/$UID .
This is the
.Em default
for LaunchAgents in
.Pa ~/Library/LaunchAgents
and
.Pa /Library/LaunchAgents
when the plist omits
.Cm LimitLoadToSessionType
(Apple's default is Aqua).
.It Ar user
Background / non-GUI user session
.Pq Cm user/$UID .
Use for agents meant for SSH-style contexts
.Pq typically Cm LimitLoadToSessionType=Background .
.It Ar system
System LaunchDaemons
.Pq Cm system .
Requires root.
.El
.Pp
.Nm
still honors an explicit
.Fl \-domain
on install and the plist's
.Cm LimitLoadToSessionType
when set
.Pq Aqua maps to gui; Background and LoginWindow map to user; System maps to system .
See also
.Xr launchctl 1
and Apple's
.Dq Daemons and Agents
technote
.Pq TN2083 .
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Nm
optionally reads YAML config from the first existing path among:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Pa ~/.lctlrc
.It
.Pa ~/Library/Application Support/lctl/.lctlrc
.It
.Pa ~/.config/lctl/.lctlrc
.El
.Pp
Config may define extra plist directories and their launchd domain:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
directories:
  - path: ~/Services
    domain: gui
  - path: /Library/LaunchDaemons
    domain: system
.Ed
.Pp
Valid
.Cm domain
values:
.Ar system ,
.Ar user ,
.Ar gui .
Paths may use
.Ql ~ .
Config is skipped when running as root
.Pq home is Pa /var/root .
.Pp
Plists in
.Pa ~/Library/Application Support/lctl/{gui,user,system}
.Po or
.Ev LCTL_CONFIG_DIR Ns Pa /{gui,user,system}
.Pc
are also scanned, with the domain taken from the subdirectory name.
.Cm install
accepts the name of one of these plists instead of a path.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
List user-visible services:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
lctl list
.Ed
.Pp
Install a plist into the GUI domain via symlink:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
lctl install ./com.example.my.plist --domain gui
.Ed
.Pp
Start, inspect, and stop a service:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
lctl start my.service
lctl status my.service
lctl logs my.service -t 1h
lctl stop my.service
.Ed
.Pp
Reload a service after editing a symlinked plist:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
lctl reload my.service
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr launchctl 1 ,
.Xr launchd 8
